body:
### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?

This happens for both tests in https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/overlapping-navigations-and-traversals/same-document-nav-cross-document-nav.html

Analysing the flow of the first test:

```javascript
promise_test(async t => {
  const iframe = await createIframe(t);

  iframe.contentWindow.location.hash = "#1";
  assert_equals(iframe.contentWindow.location.hash, "#1");

  iframe.contentWindow.location.search = "?2";
  await waitForLoad(iframe);
  assert_equals(iframe.contentWindow.location.search, "?2");
}, "fragment navigation then cross-document navigation");

```

a fragment navigation never sets ongoing navigation through it's [navigate](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#navigate) to [navigate to a fragment](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#navigate-fragid) path.

[finalize a same-document navigation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#finalize-a-same-document-navigation) is queued on the session history traversal queue. When that runs, step 8.4 of apply the history step sets the ongoing navigation to "traversal", and step 14.10.1 later sets it to null (both unconditionally).

Meanwhile the cross document location.search = "?2" navigation synchronously sets the ongoing navigation to its own navigationId in step 20 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#navigate.

With cross document navigation first setting navigation ID, the queued same-document finalization then runs afterward and 8.4 overwrites the navigationId with "traversal". Then, when the cross document navigation reaches step 24.2 of [navigate](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#navigate) the ongoing navigation is no longer its navigationId, so it is aborted, so the iframe never fires its load event, and waitForLoad waits forever.

One potential fix I was looking at at one stage was to do something like:

If navigationType is "traverse" or "reload", then set navigable's ongoing navigation to "traversal", but it would be good to understand how other engines pass this test since the ongoing navigation concept in the spec seems to potentially be a bit removed from implementations.
